  "title": "Rosalind Franklin",
  "summary": "Rosalind Franklin was a British physical chemist and X-ray crystallographer whose research at King's College London produced Photograph 51 in May 1952, revealing the helical parameters and helical symmetry of DNA. Her rigorous diffraction data were essential for James Watson and Francis Crick to build their double-helix model, and she subsequently led pioneering structural studies on plant viruses before her early death at 37.",
